    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="wrap hero">
      <p class="kicker"><b>Ashmit Bohora</b> · Austin, TX · UT Austin <b>Statistics &amp; Data Science</b> · Class of 2029</p>
      <h1><span class="sr-only">Ashmit Bohora: </span>Full-stack. <span class="lit">Literally.</span></h1>
      <p class="dek">
        I'm <b>Ashmit Bohora</b>. I rebuilt WLF Club's website and infrastructure as their GTM
        Engineer, shipped 19+ free community sites solo through Webspansion, and built production apps with
        real users (Guruji, BohoQuest). Looking for Summer 2027 internships in data science,
        software engineering, or AI.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-numbers">
        <div class="hn"><div class="n">19+</div><div class="l">live client sites shipped</div></div>
        <div class="hn"><div class="n">2</div><div class="l">products shipped to production</div></div>
        <div class="hn"><div class="n">6K+</div><div class="l">followers on my food brand</div></div>
        <div class="hn"><div class="n">3.75</div><div class="l">GPA at UT Austin</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn primary" href="#stack">See the stack</a>
        <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/ashmitbohora" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
        <a class="btn" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ashmitbohora" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
        <a class="btn" href="mailto:ashmitbohora@utexas.edu">Email me</a>
      </div>
      <p class="scroll-cue">
        scroll: each layer of the burger is <b>a layer of me</b>
        <svg class="arrow" viewBox="0 0 14 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 1v13M2 9.5L7 14.5l5-5" stroke="#B93018" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </p>
      <a class="skip-facts" href="/ashmit-bohora-resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">in a hurry? view plain resume →</a>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ scrolly: the burger unstacks as you scroll ============ -->
    <div class="scrolly" id="stack">
      <div class="wrap scrolly-grid">
        <div class="sticky-pane">
          <canvas id="burgerCanvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
          <div class="layer-tag" id="layerTag" aria-hidden="true"><b>01 / 06</b> &nbsp;TOP BUN · FRONTEND</div>
        </div>
        <div class="chapters" id="chapters">

          <section class="chapter" data-layer="0">
            <span class="tag"><span class="swatch" style="background:#DD9A4E"></span><span class="t"><b>Layer 01</b> · Top bun · Frontend</span></span>
            <h2>WLF Club</h2>
            <p class="lead">GTM Engineer. <span>Rebuilt it from the ground up.</span></p>
            <p class="body">Rebuilt wlfclub.com in-house, replacing a $15,000 agency build that still had 12 Lorem Ipsum pages live in production. Migrated the clinic's DNS to Cloudflare with zero downtime and zero mail interruption, verifying every record and SPF/DKIM/DMARC under a strict reject policy before cutover. Also built Warvis, an internal RAG assistant hosted for the whole team, and a member health portal replacing paid HeadsUp Health software.</p>
            <div class="stats">
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">30+</div><div class="l">pages rebuilt in-house</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">29</div><div class="l">DNS records verified pre-cutover</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">0</div><div class="l">downtime, zero mail interruption</div></div>
            </div>
            <figure class="proof">
              <span class="shot"><img src="/proof/wlfclub.jpg" width="1280" height="800" alt="The live WLF Club homepage: Recover Smarter, Feel Better, Live Longer" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span>
              <figcaption><span>The business behind these numbers</span><a href="https://wlfclub.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">wlfclub.com →</a></figcaption>
            </figure>
          </section>

          <section class="chapter" data-layer="1">
            <span class="tag"><span class="swatch" style="background:#55833A"></span><span class="t"><b>Layer 02</b> · Lettuce · The fresh stuff</span></span>
            <h2>Webspansion</h2>
            <p class="lead">A pro bono web studio I founded at 17. <span>19+ live sites, all free.</span></p>
            <p class="body">Accessibility-first websites built free, as community service, for nonprofits, immigrant-owned local businesses, and community groups: intake, build, deploy, handoff, all solo. Plus Python automation for image pipelines and a CRM that runs itself.</p>
            <div class="stats">
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">19+</div><div class="l">live sites shipped</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">23+</div><div class="l">SEO blog posts</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">2024</div><div class="l">founded</div></div>
            </div>
            <figure class="proof">
              <span class="shot"><img src="/proof/webspansion.jpg" width="1280" height="800" alt="The live Webspansion homepage: I build free websites. Seriously. 19 free sites delivered" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span>
              <figcaption><span>Live, with public stats</span><a href="https://getwebspansion.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">getwebspansion.org →</a></figcaption>
            </figure>
          </section>

          <section class="chapter" data-layer="2">
            <span class="tag"><span class="swatch" style="background:#F2C14E"></span><span class="t"><b>Layer 03</b> · Cheese · APIs &amp; automation</span></span>
            <h2>Prospansion</h2>
            <p class="lead">The paid arm of Webspansion. <span>Analytics, SEO, automation.</span></p>
            <p class="body">Built Prospansion Studio, a multi-tenant Cloudflare Workers + D1 CMS giving paying clients self-serve site editing: invite-only signup, hashed tokens, single-use resets, and a fixed sanitizer-bypass XSS vulnerability, verified via exploit proof-of-fix. Deployed for nonprofit client Ocura.</p>
            <div class="stats">
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">Multi-tenant</div><div class="l">Workers + D1 CMS</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">Fixed</div><div class="l">sanitizer-bypass XSS</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">Ocura</div><div class="l">live nonprofit client</div></div>
            </div>
            <figure class="proof pair">
              <div class="pair-grid">
                <div class="pf">
                  <span class="pf-label">BEFORE</span>
                  <span class="shot"><img src="/proof/ocura-before.jpg" width="1280" height="800" alt="Ocura's old site: generic template hero with an oversized logo" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span>
                </div>
                <div class="pf">
                  <span class="pf-label after">AFTER</span>
                  <span class="shot"><img src="/proof/ocura-after.jpg" width="1280" height="800" alt="Ocura redesigned: editorial layout with the real student team photo, running on Prospansion Studio" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <figcaption><span>Same nonprofit, redesigned + moved onto the CMS, now on its own domain</span><a href="https://ocuraeyehealth.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ocuraeyehealth.org →</a></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <div class="links"><a href="https://prospansion.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">prospansion.com →</a></div>
          </section>

          <section class="chapter" data-layer="3">
            <span class="tag"><span class="swatch" style="background:#C79A5B"></span><span class="t"><b>Layer 04</b> · Patty · The data</span></span>
            <h2>Local-First AI &amp; Knowledge Systems</h2>
            <p class="lead">Warvis: <span>RAG, all local.</span></p>
            <p class="body">Built Warvis, a RAG knowledge system ingesting 700+ documents into a cited, hybrid-search graph (SQLite FTS5 + local embeddings), with a HIPAA-aware PHI-scanning gate and fail-closed access control on every query (229 passing tests). Now hosted for WLF's whole team; the owner talks to it by voice to check on the business.</p>
            <p class="joke">Unrelated, but worth saying: the patty's grilled chicken, not beef. <b>I'm Hindu, so I swapped it.</b></p>
            <div class="stats">
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">700+</div><div class="l">docs ingested (Warvis)</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">229</div><div class="l">passing tests (Warvis)</div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/ashmitbohora" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="GitHub profile: Warvis">GitHub profile →</a></div>
          </section>

          <section class="chapter" data-layer="4" id="shipped">
            <span class="tag"><span class="swatch" style="background:#B93018"></span><span class="t"><b>Layer 05</b> · Special sauce · Shipped</span></span>
            <h2>Shipped Production Apps</h2>
            <p class="lead">Guruji and BohoQuest: <span>real users, real database, real tests.</span></p>
            <p class="body">Guruji (getguruji.com): a free, gamified community-education PWA (React, TypeScript, Supabase) with RLS-scoped auth and a self-run security audit against the live database, zero exploitable vulnerabilities. BohoQuest (app.bohoquest.app): a gamified check-in app (Expo/React Native) with server-side anti-cheat, Apple Sign-In, and a 121-test suite, live in TestFlight.</p>
            <div class="stats">
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">0</div><div class="l">exploitable vulns found</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">121</div><div class="l">BohoQuest test suite</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">TestFlight</div><div class="l">live status</div></div>
            </div>
            <figure class="proof">
              <span class="shot"><img src="/proof/guruji.jpg" width="1280" height="800" alt="Guruji live: a warm onboarding screen reading Your pocket guru, free, no login, 5 minutes a day" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span>
              <figcaption><span>Guruji, live in production</span><a href="https://app.getguruji.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">app.getguruji.com →</a></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <div class="links">
              <a href="https://getguruji.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">getguruji.com →</a>
              <a href="https://app.bohoquest.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">app.bohoquest.app →</a>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="chapter" data-layer="5">
            <span class="tag"><span class="swatch" style="background:#DD9A4E"></span><span class="t"><b>Layer 06</b> · Bottom bun · The foundation</span></span>
            <h2>UT Austin: Statistics &amp; Data Science</h2>
            <p class="lead">The base that holds the whole stack up. <span>Class of 2029.</span></p>
            <p class="body">3.75 GPA. QuestBridge Finalist. UT Impact Scholar ($48K merit award). Thomas &amp; Elizabeth Merner Scholarship in Natural Sciences ($2,000, 2026&ndash;2027). Currently a rising sophomore looking for Summer 2027 internships in data science, software engineering, machine learning, or AI.</p>
            <div class="stats">
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">3.75</div><div class="l">GPA</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">$48K</div><div class="l">merit scholarship</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">2027</div><div class="l">internship target</div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="links"><a href="mailto:ashmitbohora@utexas.edu">Email me →</a></div>
          </section>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ finale ============ -->
    <section class="finale-flat" id="hire">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Clean plate. <span>Hire accordingly.</span></h2>
        <p>That was the whole stack: every layer real, shipped, and explainable on a whiteboard.</p>
        <div class="cta">
          <a class="btn primary" href="mailto:ashmitbohora@utexas.edu">Email me</a>
          <a class="btn" href="/ashmit-bohora-resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Download resume</a>
          <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/ashmitbohora" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
          <a class="btn" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ashmitbohora" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ numbers ============ -->
    <section class="flat" id="numbers" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="sec-head"><span class="idx">The Numbers</span><h2>Your receipt</h2></div>
        <div class="receipt-zone">
          <div class="receipt">
            <p class="rh">ASHMIT'S</p>
            <p class="sub">ORDER #2029 · UT AUSTIN, STATS &amp; DATA SCIENCE<br>SERVER: HIMSELF · TABLE: RISING SOPHOMORE</p>
            <div class="rule"></div>
            <div class="r-row"><span>LIVE CLIENT SITES (SOLO)</span><span class="v hot">19+</span></div>
            <div class="r-row"><span>DOCS IN MY LOCAL RAG (WARVIS)</span><span class="v">700+</span></div>
            <div class="r-row"><span>FOLLOWERS ON BOHOBITES (MY FOOD BRAND)</span><span class="v">6K+</span></div>
            <div class="r-row"><span>BRANDS ON ONE VIDEO PIPELINE</span><span class="v">4</span></div>
            <div class="r-row"><span>GPA</span><span class="v">3.75</span></div>
            <div class="rule"></div>
            <div class="r-total"><span>TOTAL</span><span class="hot">HIREABLE</span></div>
            <div class="rule"></div>
            <p class="r-thanks">*** EVERY NUMBER MEASURED, NOT GARNISHED ***</p>
          </div>
          <div class="receipt-live">
            <figure class="proof">
              <span class="shot"><img src="/proof/webspansion-stats.jpg" width="1280" height="800" alt="Webspansion's public By The Numbers page: 19 of 100 websites built so far, real numbers only" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span>
              <figcaption><span>Don't take the receipt's word for it</span><a href="https://getwebspansion.org/stats" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">live stats →</a></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <p class="live-note"><b>The receipt runs live.</b> Webspansion's numbers publish to a public stats page, updated every time a site ships, on analytics infrastructure I built myself.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- TODO(ashmit): decided not to link a GitHub repo for Guruji/BohoQuest above since it's
         undecided whether those repos go public. Add one later if you make either public. -->

